# stage 2
# Carried over from stage 1 by tools/stage_names.py (src/stage1/stage1.ann): 150 of 310 named routines, the same code.
@equ $4000 Screen 6144 ; the screen's pixels
@equ $4134 EnergyBarScreen ; the HUD's energy bar: screen row 1, pixel line 1, column 20
@equ $5800 Attributes 768 ; the screen's attributes
@equ $5B00 PlayBuffer 4415 ; the play buffer $5B00-$6CFF (its tail $6C3F-$6CFF is PlayBufferTail in the block): 18 character rows of 8 lines of 32 bytes, linear; also the unpack area of StageGraphics
@equ $F959 DigitGlyphs ; resident font from '0': 8 bytes a character, 7 rows drawn (RenderDigits)
@equ $F9B0 PlaySoundVector ; resident: JP to the AY effect starter (E = the effect number)
@equ $F9BF DecimalTable 10 ; resident: the words 10000, 1000, 100, 10, 1
@equ $F9CC DissolveMasks 8 ; resident: DissolveHud's eight masks
@equ $F9FB Score 2 ; resident: the score's low four decimal digits, 0-9999 (AddScore)
@equ $F9FD ScoreHigh ; resident: the score's high two digits (ten thousands), 0-99 (AddScore)
@equ $FA00 BitReverse 256 ; resident: each byte with its bits reversed (the sprites drawn facing left)
@equ $FB00 ScreenLineTable 384 ; resident: the screen address of each of the 192 pixel lines (words)
@equ $FC90 KeyUp ; resident key reader: Z when UP is held (DEFINE KEYS / joystick patch its port and bit)
@equ $FC9F KeyDown ; resident key reader: Z when DOWN is held
@equ $FCAE KeyLeft ; resident key reader: Z when LEFT is held
@equ $FCBD KeyRight ; resident key reader: Z when RIGHT is held
@equ $FCCC KeyFire ; resident key reader: Z when FIRE is held
@equ $FCDB KeyHook ; resident: called before every key read (a RET, or the joystick / pause check DEFINE KEYS installs)
@equ $FE08 RandomSeed 2 ; NextSeed $8B76: seed = seed x 5 + $15 (a linear congruential step); $07CF at the stage start (InitStageState)
@equ $FE0A RandomPointer 2 ; Random $8B85: a pointer into the ROM ($0000-$3FFF), whose bytes are the random numbers; reseeded from R every 64 passes, $07CF at the stage start, $0D7A at each burst
@equ $FE0E SavedSP 2 ; ClearBuffer and CopyBuffer keep the caller's SP here while SP walks their buffers
@equ $FE10 InitOnly10 2 ; set to 2 by InitStageState $9766; SpawnHarpy $8DA4 keeps IY here (a word) between its two SpawnActor calls
@equ $FE12 InitOnly12 ; set to 1 by InitStageState; no stage-2 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE14 WorkByte ; scratch: the placement counter of LoadRoomActors, the shape bits of StartBurst
@equ $FE17 ItemSelected ; the slot of CarriedItems the HUD cursor is on (6 at the start)
@equ $FE18 ItemLast ; the last used slot of CarriedItems (6 at the start; AddItem raises it)
@equ $FE19 ItemFirst ; the first slot of CarriedItems (6): the item window does not scroll before it
@equ $FE1C SpanCount 2 ; the spans in the span table $76A0 that CopyBuffer copies (BuildSpans $99E9)
@equ $FE1E SpanRow ; BuildSpans' cell row 0-17
@equ $FE1F CellColumn ; the cell column 2-29 of RoomChange's and BuildSpans' loops
@equ $FE21 RoomColumn ; the room's left edge in the grid, in blocks (2 cells)
@equ $FE22 RoomRow ; the room's top edge in the grid, in blocks (16 lines)
@equ $FE23 RoomGrid 2 ; the grid record of the current map grid ($9B6F, $9B8A or $9B96)
@equ $FE25 Placements 2 ; the current grid's placement list (Grid0Placements, Grid1Placements, Grid2Placements): 3 bytes a placement, $FF ends
@equ $FE27 MissileCursor ; AddMissile's round-robin slot number 0-7
@equ $FE29 CellFlag ; PutBlock $9986: the byte written to the cell's twin in $7040 (always 0)
@equ $FE2E RoomExitsPtr 2 ; the current room's byte in the grid's room table (grid record +4 + RoomNumber)
@equ $FE30 RoomNumber ; the room in its grid, a grid row of rooms after another: +1 right, -1 left, + grid record +8 down (stage 1, grid 0: 12 the demon's lair)
@equ $FE31 PassCounter ; +1 every pass (PassTick $984D): the animations' clock
@equ $FE37 InitOnly3A ; stage 1 has it at $FE3A; set to $10 by InitStageState $9766; no stage-2 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE3A BurstTimer ; stage 1 has it at $FE3D; the burst's step 0..$1B ($0D in the small mode); $64 idle (RoomChange sets it), $FF just started
@equ $FE3B BurstSmall ; stage 1 has it at $FE3E; 0 a big burst (28 steps), 1 a small one (14 steps, doubled direction steps)
@equ $FE3C Energy ; stage 1 has it at $FE3F; the hero's energy, 0 (full) to $2E
@equ $FE3E InitOnly40 ; stage 1 has it at $FE40; set to $0D by InitStageState $9766; no stage-2 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE3F InitOnly41 ; stage 1 has it at $FE41; set to 1 by InitStageState $9766; no stage-2 code reads it (known only from the code)
@equ $FE40 SpanOpen ; stage 1 has it at $FE42; BuildSpans $93B5: 1 while a run of open cells goes on
@equ $FE43 Hydra1Step ; the hydra's first head: its step 0-$14 (HydraNeck1Step $9EEC); HydraHead1Actor $7FB5 fires at steps 4, 8 and 12 ($B31C)
@equ $FE53 ItemsChanged ; stage 1 has it at $FE4A; 1 after AddItem $7E2B: the main loop redraws the item strip (RedrawItemsIfChanged $7CF1)
@equ $FE54 GridNumber ; stage 1 has it at $FE4B; the grid the hero is in: 0 Grid0 (the temple and the hydra's rooms), 1 Grid1, 2 Grid2 (Medusa's room); set by EnterGrid1 $8814, EnterGrid2 $8835, LeaveGrid2 $8859, LeaveGrid1 $8882
@equ $FE58 EnergyShown ; stage 1 has it at $FE4D; the energy the HUD bar last drew
@equ $FE59 EnergyChange ; stage 1 has it at $FE4E; the pending energy change: $80 and up drains 2 a pass, under $80 refills 2 a pass
@equ $FE5B SpawnDelay ; stage 1 has it at $FE4F; SpawnTimer $8D45: passes to the next random spawn (5-20; a random byte at the stage start)
@equ $FE60 FireLatch ; stage 1 has it at $FE50; 1 while FIRE stays held after a shot or a throw: one a press
@equ $FE6B PiecesMask ; stage 1 has it at $FE51; one bit a piece of the artefact (the room event's bit, actor +$10): spawned and taken
@equ $FE6A PiecesTaken ; stage 1 has it at $FE52; pieces taken, 0-5
@equ $FE62 PieceFlash ; stage 1 has it at $FE53; passes left of the HUD pieces' colour flash
@equ $FE69 PiecesComplete ; stage 1 has it at $FE54; set to 1 when the fifth piece is taken; +1 for each item of kind 6 taken (SpawnRewardItem gives the kind-6 item while it is 1)
@equ $FE63 PieceTakenFlag ; stage 1 has it at $FE55; 1 for one pass after a piece is taken
@equ $FE64 RespawnShiftX ; stage 1 has it at $FE56; $FF: no death pending; else the hero's column less the respawn column less 2 (HeroDeath $B22B); the path flyers move by it (x 2) when their path ends
@equ $FE65 RespawnShiftY ; stage 1 has it at $FE57; the hero's line less the respawn line less $27, set with RespawnShiftX
@equ $FE66 HeroFreeze ; stage 1 has it at $FE58; passes the hero's state handler is skipped ($17 after a life lost, LoseLife $7EA8)
@equ $FE6C LivesFlash ; stage 1 has it at $FE59; the lives boxes' flash step, 0-$10 ($10 idle)
@equ $FE68 RestoreAttributes ; stage 1 has it at $FE5A; 1: UpdateAttributes takes the solid cells' colours from RoomAttributes once (the new room fades in over the old one)
@equ $FE6D GameOverTimer ; stage 1 has it at $FE5B; 0 in play; 1 when the last life is lost, counts to $32
@equ $FE5C Hydra1Neck ; the first head's neck ($0E at the start; written by $9EEC); bit 7 set: the head cut off (CutHydraHead1 $80C1), $80 the head gone (its actors removed)
@equ $FE5D Hydra2Neck ; the second head's neck ($16 at the start; written by $9F31); bit 7 as Hydra1Neck
@equ $FE5E Hydra3Neck ; the third head's neck ($0E at the start; written by $9F75); bit 7 as Hydra1Neck
@equ $FE5F HydraHeads ; the hydra's heads left: 3 at the start, - 1 for each head cut off ($80C1, $80D6, $80EB); $64 once HydraDefeated $9BB4 has burst the body
@equ $FE6F Lives ; stage 1 has it at $FE61; lives left, from H at StageEntry
@equ $FE41 Hydra3Step ; the third head's step (written by $9F75), as Hydra1Step
@equ $FE42 Hydra3Pose ; the third head's pose (written by $9F75), as Hydra1Pose
@equ $FE44 Hydra1Pose ; the first head's pose from $A113 (written by $9EEC): PlaceHydraHead $8100 picks its frame by it (under 5, 5-6, 7 and up)
@equ $FE45 Hydra2Step ; the second head's step (written by $9F31), as Hydra1Step
@equ $FE46 Hydra2Pose ; the second head's pose (written by $9F31), as Hydra1Pose
@equ $FE4D Hydra1X ; the first head's x in pixels less $18 ($28 at the start; written by $9EAE): PlaceHydraHead's column and shift
@equ $FE4E Hydra1Y ; the first head's line ($15 at the start; written by $9EAE)
@equ $FE4F Hydra2X ; the second head's x, as Hydra1X ($6D at the start)
@equ $FE50 Hydra2Y ; the second head's line ($11 at the start)
@equ $FE51 Hydra3X ; the third head's x, as Hydra1X ($34 at the start)
@equ $FE52 Hydra3Y ; the third head's line ($0E at the start)
@equ $FE55 Statue0Broken ; 1 once the statue of kind 0 ($A6EC) is struck: BreakStatue0 $9A41; the statue is not placed again
@equ $FE56 Statue1State ; the statue of kind 1 ($A718): 0 standing, 1-3 the flash after a blow, $C8 broken (BreakStatue1 $9A14)
@equ $FE57 MedusaState ; 0 Medusa stands, 1 struck (MedusaStruck $8138: her head falls), 2 the head lies, 4 the head taken (an item); CheckMedusaBarrier $835D closes the way at column $18 while 0
@equ $FE5A HarpyPhase ; the harpy's statue (kind 3, $A7F6): 3 once the harpy is out (SpawnHarpy $8DA4), $FA when it flies off ($8EA9), back to 1 from 3 when the hero leaves the room (LeaveRoomRight / Left)
@equ $FE67 SpiritCount ; the spirits (SpawnRandomEnemy $8F8C, SpiritActor $9028) on screen, at most 2
@inline $8C63 5
@inline $8C93 5
@inline $AC52
@module variables ; The stage's work space: the play buffer's tail, the shadow attributes, the HUD picture and the records over it
@about The block's first 5057 bytes ($6C3F-$77FF) are loaded with the stage but hold no code; they are laid out as stage 1's (the HUD picture $7000-$76BF is the same 1728 bytes as stage 1's). $6C3F-$6CFF is the end of the play buffer PlayBuffer ($5B00-$6CFF: 18 character rows of 8 lines of 32 bytes, linear), $6D00-$6FFF the shadow of the screen's attributes. $7000-$76BF holds, as loaded, the HUD: its picture (48 lines of 32 bytes, linear) and its colours (6 rows of 32). StageSetUp $9177 copies the colours into the shadow and DissolveHud $8AD6 the picture onto the screen once, at the stage's start; then the space is reused: the old room's colours, the room's cells, the 14 actor records, the 16 missile records, the score's digit picture and the span table.
@about An actor record (18 bytes, the hero's at $74E0 and 13 at $74F2) is stage 1's: +0 X (byte column 0-29; $FF a free record), +1 Y (line in the play buffer), +2 width in bytes, +3 height in lines, +4/+5 the frame's bitmap, +6/+7 the handler, +8 the frame or a counter, +9 flags (bit 0 opaque, bit 4 hit, bit 7 facing left), +$0A the state, +$0B the item kind or a step, +$0C the attribute, +$0D/+$0E the base X and Y, +$0F kept over a room change, +$10 the placement's number or a counter, +$11 the pixel shift (PreShiftSprite $7F10).
$6C3F s PlayBufferTail ; The last 193 bytes of the play buffer PlayBuffer $5B00-$6CFF (character row 17's last lines)
> ClearBuffer $9484 clears the play buffer to $6CFF with PUSH HL (SP from $6D00); RoomChange $9257 unpacks the stage's tiles and map into it from $5B00 (3852 bytes, to $6A0B); the actors are drawn into it every pass. Zero as loaded. Read and written in s2-right and rzx-r2 (CopyBuffer $94A9 copies it out).

$6D00 s ShadowAttributes ; The shadow of the screen's 768 attributes, the screen's layout; the play area from $6DC2 (row 6, column 2)
> The HUD's colours are copied into rows 0-5 at the stage's set-up (StageSetUp $9177); RoomChange $9257 writes each cell's attribute into rows 6-23, the actors' colours are painted over them every pass, and UpdateAttributes $8CD0 copies the open cells to $5800 (ShowShadowAttributes $8CC3 the whole of it). FillShadowAttributes $8C93 paints rectangles into it with five bytes after its CALL. Zero as loaded.
$6DC0 PlayAttributes ; row 6: the first row of the play area (the room's 18 rows)
$6DC2 PlayAttributesCell ; row 6, column 2: the room's first cell

$7000 b HudPicture 32 ; The HUD as loaded: 48 lines of 32 bytes (linear, top first), then their colours at $7600 (6 rows of 32)
> DissolveHud $8AD6 dissolves the 48 lines onto the screen's lines 0-47 and StageSetUp $9177 copies the 192 colours into the shadow rows 0-5, once, at the stage's start. EndStage $789D saves the screen's lines 0-47 back here and the attributes $5800-$58BF to $7600 when the stage ends, so the next stage's block shows the HUD as the player left it. The same 1728 bytes as stage 1's HudPicture (src/res/stage2/picture-hud-32x48.png).
$7040 RoomAttributes ; $7040-$727F: the old room's play colours (SavePlayAttrs $99C2: 576 bytes, rows 6-23) and the cells' twins; also the burst's particles (StartBurst $9BFA, 4 bytes each, read by UpdateBurst $9C92)
$7042 RoomAttributesCell ; the twin of the cell $7282 (576 bytes lower)
$7280 Cells ; the room's cells: 19 rows of 32 (tile numbers, then their kinds after BuildSpans $93B5; bit 1 solid, bit 3 deadly)
$7282 CellsPlay ; row 0, column 2: the room's first cell (RoomCells $92F4 writes 28 x 18)
$74C0 CellsFloor ; row 18 below the room: 32 bytes of $FF (StartGrid $A35D), a floor no actor falls through
$74E0 HeroRecord ; the hero's actor record (18 bytes; +0 X)
$74E1 HeroY ; +1 the hero's line
$74E8 HeroFrame ; +8 the frame number of the hero's set
$74E9 HeroFlags ; +9 bit 7: facing left
$74EA HeroState ; +$0A the hero's state (stage 1's numbering)
$74EC HeroAttribute ; +$0C the hero's attribute
$74ED HeroBaseX ; +$0D the base column
$74EE HeroBaseY ; +$0E the base line
$74F0 HeroCounter ; +$10 the pause after a death
$74F2 Actors ; the 13 other actor records, 18 bytes each ($74F2-$75DB); +0 = $FF a free record
$75CA LastActor ; the 13th record
$75DC ActorsEnd ; 4 bytes past the records (written and read in rzx-r2: a 15th record's first bytes are tested as the list's end)
$75E0 Missiles ; the 16 missile records, 6 bytes each ($75E0-$763F): +0 the column ($FF free), +1 the line, +2 the kind, +3 to +5 the kind's own
$7600 HudColours ; the HUD's 192 colours as loaded (rows 0-5); in play the missile records 4-15 lie over them
$7610 MissilesHigh ; missile records 8-15 (AddMissileHigh $B3C5)
$7640 DigitBuffer ; in play: the score's digit picture and a sprite's shifted copy (PreShiftSprite $7F10)
$76A0 SpanTable ; in play: the open spans CopyBuffer $94A9 copies, 6 bytes each (the length, 0, the buffer address, the screen address), on to $77B9
@res stage2/picture-hud-32x48.bin

$76C0 s SpanTableRest ; The span table's room past the HUD's colours: spans 6-46 ($76C0-$77B9)
> BuildSpans $93B5 and AddSpan $943D write the spans from $76A0 on; rzx-r2 fills them to $77B9 (47 spans; stage 1's recordings reached $779B). Zero as loaded.

$77BA s Unused77BA ; 70 bytes no code reads or writes (s2-right, rzx-r2); zero as loaded

@module entry ; The stage's entry and set-up
@about Stage 2's block is entered at $7800 by the resident stage loader with H = the lives. StageEntry sets up the stage (variables, title, HUD, the first room of grid 0) and falls into the main loop; EndStage returns to the loader with E = the outcome (0 game over, 1 quit, 2 stage completed), H = the lives and BC = the score's digits. In rzx-r2 the stage runs from frame 26 to frame 19011 (EndStage with E = 2 after the exit effect at frame 18721); in s2-right it ends in game over (EndStage at frame 5826).
$7800 c StageEntry ; Start the stage: lives from H, variables, HUD, the first room, then the main loop
> Called by the resident stage loader ($F239) with H = the lives left. Stores H in Lives, then: InitStageState $9766 (clears $FE08-$FE6D, the carried items from StartItems, the energy refill), StageSetUp (the title, the HUD), ClearActors $8EEA, ResetObjectLists, RoomGrid = $953E (grid 0) and Placements = Grid0Placements, ReviveAllPlacements, $A396, StartGrid, RoomEvents $8381 (the first room's bonus checks), ClearBuffer, RunActorHandlers, DrawActors, CopyBuffer and StageFadeIn, then runs on into MainLoop.
> As in stage 1 at $7800 with stage 2's own set-up calls; stage 1's RoomNumber = 2 start is done by StartGrid here.
> Witness: L1 3 (rzx-r2, s2-right, stageload).
@module mainloop ; The main loop and its pass
@about MainLoop $7837 runs one game step a pass, with no frame sync: rzx-r2 makes 5806 passes in frames 402-18721 (about 3.2 frames a pass), s2-right 1951 passes in frames 402-5823 (2.8). Stage 2 has no busy-wait pacing: PacePassEmpty is a bare RET. A pass ends with SPACE (the item window), CAPS SHIFT + SPACE (quit) or the end of the lives.
$7837 c MainLoop ; One pass: HUD, input, actors, draw, copy; SPACE opens the item window
> The pass, in order: PacePassEmpty, ShowPieceTaken, FlashPieces, CheckPause (ENTER), SpawnTimer $8D45, RedrawItemsIfChanged, ClearBuffer, CheckStageExit (may leave to EndStage), UpdateMissiles, $9EAE, RunActorHandlers, $9E4F, DrawActors, $9E21, $9C92, HydraDefeated $9BB4, KeyHook, UpdateAttributes $8CD0 (attributes and CopyBuffer), PassTick (energy, lives flash, game over step), ShowScore, then the SPACE test TestSpaceKey.
> SPACE with CAPS SHIFT ends the stage with E = 1 (QuitStage); SPACE alone opens ItemWindow unless the hero is in state $0F (dying; the hero record's +$0A at $74EA). The loop goes on while Lives is not 0 or the hero's state is not 0; with no lives and the hero back in state 0 it ends with E = 0 (GameOverExit). rzx-r2 opened the item window 18 times; s2-right ends in game over at frame 5823.
> Witness: L1 8032 (rzx-r2, s2-right, stageload).
$7878 MainLoopSpace ; SPACE pressed: CAPS SHIFT too quits, else the item window
$7889 MainLoopNext ; go on while lives are left or the hero is not back in state 0
$7897 c GameOverExit ; No lives: end the stage with E = 0
> Reached from MainLoop when Lives and the hero's state $74EA are both 0. E = 0, then EndStage. s2-right ends so (frame 5823).
> Witness: L1 1 (s2-right).
$789B c QuitStage ; CAPS SHIFT + SPACE: end the stage with E = 1
> Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: s2-right, rzx-r2); known only from the code ($787F).
$789D c EndStage ; Leave the stage: hide the pieces boxes, then save the HUD and return (EndStageSave)
> E (pushed) is the outcome: 0 game over (GameOverExit), 1 quit (QuitStage), 2 stage completed (StageExit). Clears the play buffer, then sets the attributes of the two rows of the pieces boxes (cells $5879-$587E and $5899-$589E) to 1 (blue on black) with two LDIR fills where stage 1 used FillAttributes; runs on into EndStageSave. Reached in rzx-r2 at frame 18883 (from StageExit) and in s2-right at the game over.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r2, s2-right).
$78BB c EndStageSave ; EndStage, continued: save the HUD, clear its fields, fade, return
> Part of EndStage, after the second inline record.
> As in stage 1 at $78B2, the same code.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r2, s2-right).
@module render ; The renderer: the sprite row plotters, the play buffer, the attributes, ClearBuffer and CopyBuffer
$792E c FlashFadeScreen ; Fade every coloured ink up to white over 7 frames, then down to black over 7 frames
> Seven times (HALT each): every attribute whose ink is neither 0 nor 7 gets ink + 1. Then seven times (two HALTs each): every ink not 0 gets ink - 1. Inputs: none; changes the whole attribute area $5800-$5AFF. Called by EndStage.
> As in stage 1 at $7925, the same code.
> Witness: L1 2 (rzx-r2, s2-right).
$7930 FadeUpFrame
$7938 FadeUpCell
$7942 FadeUpNext
$794D FadeDownFrame
$7956 FadeDownCell
$795C FadeDownNext
@module mainloop
$7966 c PacePassEmpty ; The pass's pacing slot: a bare RET in stage 2
> MainLoop calls it first in every pass, where stage 1 calls PacePass (the random reseed and the busy wait of the light rooms). Stage 2 has neither: the byte is a RET.
> Witness: L1 8032 (rzx-r2, s2-right, stageload).
$7967 c CheckPause ; ENTER pauses: wait for its release, a second press and its release
> Reads port $BFFE bit 0 (ENTER). Not pressed: returns at once. Pressed: waits for the key's release, the next press and its release, so the game stands still between two presses. No other effect.
> As in stage 1 at $79B1, the same code.
> Witness: L1 8032 (rzx-r2, s2-right, stageload).
$796F PauseRelease
$7975 PausePress
$797B PauseRelease2
@module render
$7982 c CopyToScreen ; Copy a block of bytes to the screen, line by line
> Inputs: HL = the source, B = the screen column, C = the first pixel line, D = the width in bytes, E = the lines, A = the source's stride (added to HL after each line; 0 repeats one source line, used with the cleared buffer to clear a screen block). Patches the column into $799B and the stride into $79AC, then for each line takes the line's address from ScreenLineTable and LDIRs D bytes. Destroys IX, BC, DE.
> As in stage 1 at $79CC, the same code.
> Witness: L1 8701 (rzx-r2, s2-right, stageload).
$7995 CopyToScreenLine
@module hud ; The energy, the lives, the score, the HUD, game over and the stage exit
$79B2 c CheckStageExit ; With item 5 selected, standing at x 12-15 of grid 0's room 0: leave the stage
> Every pass. Only in grid 0 (GridNumber 0), room 0 (RoomNumber) and with item 5 selected (GetSelectedItem): when the hero's x ($74E0) is 12-15 and its state ($74EA) is 0, drops its own return address and runs StageExit. Stage 1's check is the same with item 6, room 2, x 18-21 and y $5A. In rzx-r2 it leaves at frame 18721 (the temple's first room with the completed artefact, item 5, selected).
> Witness: L1 8032 (rzx-r2, s2-right, stageload).
$79D3 c StageExit ; The stage's exit effect: falling stars over a coloured field until FIRE or SPACE, then EndStage with E = 2
> StartStageExit draws the field and seeds 80 stars at $5B00 (4 bytes each); then each frame (HALT) moves the stars of speed 1-3 (MoveStar), until KeyFire or SPACE ($8A79); then E = 2 and EndStage.
> As in stage 1 at $7A1D, the same code.
> Witness: L1 1 (rzx-r2).
$79D7 StageExitFrame
$79DE StageExitStar
$79FB StageExitDone
$7A00 c MoveStar ; Move one star down by its speed and plot it as two pixel lines
> IX = the star: +0 speed 1-4, +1 the pixel within the byte 0-3, +2 the column 2-29, +3 y ($80 and up: not yet on screen). Off screen: y += speed only. On screen: y = (y + speed) mod 128, clears the bytes above it (speed lines, from ScreenLineTable+96, line 48 down), and plots two lines from StarPixels (speed and pixel). Called by StageExit for each of the 80 stars every frame: rzx-r2 frames 18729-18883.
> As in stage 1 at $7A4A, the same code.
> Witness: L1 8990 (rzx-r2).
$7A0E MoveStarOnScreen ; on screen: y + speed, wrapped at 128
$7A17 MoveStarPlot ; the line address from ScreenLineTable, the pattern from StarPixels
$7A40 MoveStarClear ; clear the speed lines above the star
$7A71 b StarPixels 8 ; The two pixel lines of a star, by speed (rows 1-4) and pixel (pairs 0-3)
> Four rows of 8 bytes, one a speed 1-4; each row holds 4 pairs (the two pixel lines of a star at pixel 0-3 of the byte). Read by MoveStar ($7A39). Read in rzx-r2 at the stage's exit.
$7A91 c StartStageExit ; Clear the play area, colour it at random and seed 80 stars
> ClearPlayBuffer, then clears 144 screen lines from line 48 (ScreenLineTable+96), 30 bytes each from the line's start, directly on the screen; FillAttributes with the inline record at $7AB2 (column 2, line $30, 28 x 18 cells, attribute 0), RandomPlayAttrs, and 80 star records at $5B00: speed 1-4, pixel 0-3, column 2-29, y $80-$FF (random bytes from Random). Runs once in rzx-r2, frame 18721.
> Witness: L1 1 (rzx-r2).
$7A9A StartStageExitLine ; the next screen line
$7AA7 StartStageExitByte ; clear 30 bytes
$7AC0 SeedStar ; one star: speed and pixel
$7AD2 SeedStarColumn ; a random column 0-27 (retry on 28-31), + 2
$7AF3 c RandomPlayAttrs ; Fill the play area's attributes (28 x 16 cells) with bright inks 2-7 on black
> From $58C2 (row 6, column 2), 16 rows of 28 cells: bright, ink 2-7 from $8BAC, paper 0. Sets RandomPointer to $091D first, so the colours are the same each time.
> As in stage 1 at $7B27, the same code.
> Witness: L1 1 (rzx-r2).
$7AFF RandomPlayAttrsRow
$7B02 RandomPlayAttrsCell
$7B03 RandomPlayAttrsPick
$7B1F c AddScore ; Add BC points to the score
> Score += BC; at 10000 or more, Score -= 10000 and ScoreHigh += 1 (wrapping from 99 to 0). Outputs none; A, BC, HL destroyed. Called by UpdatePieceActor ($84DB, 1200 for a piece), ScoreBurst20 ($99E4), ItemHandler ($9AD9) and $AB4E. rzx-r2 adds 34 times (frames 913-17492); the score passes 10000 once.
> As in stage 1 at $7B53, the same code.
