@module rooms
$A33D c Unrle ; Unpack an RLE block: the first byte is the escape, ESC n v is n copies of v, ESC ESC ends
> Input: HL = the packed block, DE = the output. The block's first byte is its escape byte, written into UnrleEscape and UnrleEnd's compares. Then: a byte other than the escape is copied; the escape followed by n, v writes n copies of v (n = 0 gives 256); the escape twice ends. Output: HL = the second escape of the end mark, DE = after the output.
> RoomChange $9257 ($9262) unpacks the stage's tiles and map StageGraphics $B7D5 to $5B00 with it at every room change (7 calls in s2-right, 33 in rzx-r2).
> As in stage 1 at $A424, the same code.
> Witness: L1 43 (rzx-r2, s2-right, stageload).
$A345 UnrleNext
$A347 UnrleEscape ; CP n: n = the block's escape byte (written above)
$A34F UnrleRun
$A350 UnrleEnd ; CP n: n = the escape byte (written above)
$A357 UnrleRunLoop
$A35D c StartGrid ; Clear the room cells and the actors' extra state, enter the current grid at its start room, build it
> Clears $7280-$74BF (the room's cells), fills $74C0-$74DF with $FF, calls $921E, then reads the RoomGrid record: RoomColumn = +2, RoomRow = +3, RoomExitsPtr = +4/+5 (the grid's room table), and jumps to RoomChange $9257. Called at the stage start (StageEntry $7822) and by EnterGridBuild $ADBA at each grid change (1 in s2-right, 6 in rzx-r2).
> As in stage 1 at $A444, the same code.
> Witness: L1 10 (rzx-r2, s2-right, stageload).
