> As in stage 1 at $AA3E, the same code.
> Witness: L1 8034 (rzx-r2, s2-right, stageload).
$ACB7 c CheckHeroFooting ; Catch a ledge in a jump, or start a fall where the ground ends
> IY = the hero. In a jump (state 2) at frame $0C: solid ground under the feet one column ahead (CellUnderFeet $B282, E = 1, D = 2) lands him on the ledge: frame $0F, the base column 2 back, the base line 16 up ($8F84), on into the jump's frame (JumpFrame $B1ED); at frame $0F with no ground there he drops (StartDrop $B01D). Standing (state 0) or walking (state 1) at frame 5 or $0B with no ground under him (E = 2, D = 0) starts a fall (StartFall $B00B).
> As in stage 1 at $AA67, the same instructions; the operands the draft marked are the same numbers (the frames, the offsets) and the routines' new addresses: nothing of the stage.
