@module rooms
$B7D5 b StageGraphics 16 ; The stage's tiles, blocks and map, RLE-packed (3072 bytes; 3852 unpacked: 195 tiles, 110 blocks, the three grids' map of 1452 bytes)
> RoomChange $9257 unpacks it with Unrle $A33D into the play buffer at $5B00 at every room change. Unrle as in stage 1: the first byte is the escape ($C9 here); a byte other than the escape is itself, ESC n v is n copies of v, ESC ESC ends. The unpacked block: five words (the offsets of the tile kinds, pixels, attributes, blocks and map from $5B0A), then the five sections.
> The packer that made it is greedy (every run of 4 to 255 equal bytes is ESC n v) except one stretch of 8 zero bytes left as they are (unpacked offset 1397, a blank tile's pixels); with that one exception tools/res_stage.py packs the block again bit for bit. graphics.txt holds the escape, the stretch, the tile kinds, the blocks and the map (GRIDS['stage2'] in tools/res_stage.py: 69 x 9, 47 x 15, 14 x 9), tiles.png the tiles' pixels and colours. Read whole in s2-right and rzx-r2.
@res stage2/graphics.bin

@module graphics ; The stage's sprites, pictures and their frame tables
@about Every animated actor shows frames of a sprite set: the bitmaps, then a frame table of 6-byte records (dx, dy, the width in bytes, the height in lines, the bitmap's offset from the set's start). SetActorFrame $AC52 takes the frame number in A and the table and the set from the four bytes after its CALL (or from a word pair such as StatueSet $A714). The other pictures are plain 1-bit frames read through their addresses: the shots, the hydra's heads, necks and body, the harpy's body, the item icons, the drifting shots, the burst's glyphs and shapes.
@about The layout follows stage 1's (shots, game over, the urns, the hero's strikes, the energy bar, the hero's jump and walk, the fragments, the pieces, the item icons, the drifting shots, the hero's leap, the burst tables), with stage 2's own sets between: the spirit, the pool's ripple, the hydra's necks, heads and body, Medusa, the harpy and its wings, lamp and rise, the statues, the sparkle, the pool and the drops. The block ends with 301 zero bytes. Every file is under src/res/stage2/ (README.md there).
$C3D5 b SpiritSprites 8 ; The spirit: 8 frames, growing out of the floor (0-5) and flapping (6, 7) (SpiritActor $9028)
> SpiritFrameSet $9050 (SetActorFrame's inline words). All 507 bytes read in s2-right and rzx-r2.
$C5A0 SpiritFrameTable ; 8 records
@res stage2/sprites-spirit.bin

